  "question": {
    "text": "The number of solutions of <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> in the interval <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />As <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous and increasing, it has exactly one root in the interval <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2,1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0077_4d7e6c3c7426.jpg\" style=\"width: 218px; height: 113px;\" />"
  }
